[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:95. A Fantasy]
[00:01.160]Passage 95 | 文章九十五
[00:02.890]A fantasy. | 幻想
[00:05.105]When the ambassador of Escalopia returned home for lunch, | 当埃斯卡洛比亚大使回家吃午饭时，
[00:10.250]his wife got a shock. | 他的妻子吓了一跳。
[00:12.755]He looked pale, | 他脸色苍白，
[00:14.855]and his clothes were in a frightful state. | 衣服也乱糟糟的。
[00:18.015]"What has happened?" she asked. | “发生什么事了？”她问道。
[00:21.105]"How did your clothes get into such a mess?" | “你的衣服怎么会弄得这么乱？”
[00:24.565]"A fire extinguisher, my dear," | “灭火器，亲爱的，”
[00:27.645]answered the ambassador dryly. | 大使干巴巴地回答。
[00:30.275]"University students set the embassy on fire this morning." | “今天早上，大学生们把大使馆给烧了。”
[00:35.225]"Good heavens," exclaimed his wife. | “天哪！”他的妻子惊呼道。
[00:39.090]"And where were you at the time?" | “那你当时在哪里？”
[00:41.925]"I was in my office, as usual," | “我像往常一样在办公室里，”
[00:44.840]answered the ambassador. | 大使回答道。
[00:46.580]"The fire broke out in the basement. | “火灾是在地下室爆发的。
[00:49.400]I went down immediately, of course, | 我当然立刻下去了，
[00:52.365]and that fool host aimed a fire extinguisher at me. | 那个愚蠢的宿主竟然把灭火器对准了我。
[00:56.840]He thought I was on fire. | 他以为我着火了。
[00:59.225]I must definitely get that fellow posted." | 我一定要把那家伙调走。”
[01:03.745]The ambassador's wife went on asking questions, | 大使的妻子继续提问，
[01:08.290]when she suddenly noticed a big hole in her husband's hat. | 突然她发现丈夫的帽子上有一个大洞。
[01:13.225]"And how can you explain that?" she asked. | “那这个你怎么解释？”她问道。
[01:18.010]"Oh, that," | “哦，那个，”
[01:19.655]said the ambassador. | 大使说。
[01:21.450]"Someone fired a shot through my office window. | “有人从我的办公室窗户开了一枪。
[01:25.305]Accurate, don't you think? | 挺准的，你不觉得吗？
[01:27.800]Fortunately, I wasn't wearing it at the time. | 幸运的是，当时我没有戴着它。
[01:31.540]If I had been, I would not have been able to get home for lunch." | 如果我戴了，我就不能回家吃午饭了。”